Riverdale is an undeniable hit and  there's a lot about the show that really  works when it's firing on all cylinders  as with anything though there are also  plenty of things that don't quite land  to appreciate them both  it's time to talk about the best and the  worst things about the show one of the  reasons Archie comics have endured for  so long as their reliance on broad  character archetypes if you take  characters with clear-cut traits and  apply them in the right way you can  essentially tell a story in any genre  you want the TV series has embraced this  from the very beginning and the result  is a show nimble enough to pivot between  horror comedy musical and crime drama  often within the space of a single  episode the flexibility with which  Riverdale can dip into many different  genres and themes means it can also  successfully juggle many different plots  at once when this is done right you get  an extremely satisfying story with a  long arc in just the right amount of  tension unfortunately season two's black  hood story wasn't quite so well juggled  it seemed to wrap up midway through the  season only to be clumsily rolled out  again for an even bigger reveal later on  sometimes Riverdale should let these  things go sooner Riverdale ostensibly  has four main characters or at least it  did when it started Archie Betty Jughead  and Veronica they're the two guys in two  girls who ultimately formed the two  couples at the heart of the show while  everyone else around them serves a  supporting role however one supporting  character has become absolutely  essential the majestic and deliciously  venomous Cheryl blossom played by  Madeline Peck  mr. Rogers nice haircut looking  extremely dilthey today is our deal  cheryl enters the series as the spoiled  rich girl who gets to be the center of  attention because her brother died and  ultimately evolves into so much more  patches gloriously indulgent performance  means cheryl also gets to steal pretty  much every scene she's in listen up  ragamuffins i will not allow a real  highs above average GPA to suffer  because of classrooms that are  overcrowded with underachievers this is  a character who can introduce herself  without a hint of irony as Riverdale's  resident it girl in one scene and then  melt your heart with vulnerability in  the next she's just that good  one of the very first things we learn  about Riverdale's version of Archie  Andrews football star and resident good  boy of Riverdale high school is that  he's been having an affair with one of  his teachers it's a sexy unexpected  element that adds a little hint of  danger to a character we think we know  and it sets Archie off on a promising  path to being much more than the Queen  cut boy next door in the years since  then  Archie's become even darker and so  Archie always trying to do the good  noble thing took another step further  into darkness and yet despite all these  steps into darkness he still remains the  least interesting main character on a  show in which he's supposed to be the  lead when the first footage of Riverdale  arrived many viewers were quick to  compare its visual tone to Twin Peaks  David Lynch and Mark Frost legendary TV  show  indeed Riverdale's first major storyline  did seem pretty Twin Peaks  esque the show's drifted even farther  into the horrific in season two and it's  made Riverdale even more fun to watch  its killings the main Riverdale cast  aside there's another group of key  supporting players josie and the  pussycats the trouble is when  Riverdale's version of josie often has a  bigger role to play as a supporting cast  member the Pussycats as a unit don't get  used very often even in some of the  show's more music heavy moments they're  pushed aside in favor of the main cast  which is a real shame hopefully they get  more to do in future episodes this year  we'd like to build on that success  continue telling our story with songs we  write Riverdale is a show packed with  high stakes stories a murder needs to be  solved a vigilante is roaming the  streets there's a gang war brewing on  the south side it works both because of  the show's sincere desire to tell these  stories and all their juicy soapy glory  and because of its commitment to  remaining tongue-in-cheek about just how  Sofia can get that means that in  addition to deeply emotional and even  terrifying moments we get dark Betty in  a black wig or Cheryl bringing the  cheerleading squad to a funeral in a  tire that could best be described as  spirit mourning  Riverdale is never afraid to have fun  with itself and that makes it more  enjoyable all around when he was first  introduced Jughead Jones was the kind of  Greek chorus of Riverdale a narrator  filling in the viewer on the shows  various shenanigans  I'm the damaged loner outsider from the  wrong side of the tracks  then as the Jason blossom story wound  down  Jughead became a guy who got mixed up in  his father's biker gang and has been one  of the strangest characters on the show  since then and the characters on words  I'm weird I'm a weirdo I don't fit in  and I don't want to fit in have you ever  seen me without the stupid hat on that's  weird  [Music]
 

